---
// Methodology & Evaluation — the contextual depth page (Workstream F, per
// docs/harbor-ridge-methodology-evaluation-implementation-brief.md, final
// revised, approved by Ken and ChatGPT), corrected per Ken and Claude
// Chat's browser-informed review pass. Answers the cold hiring-manager
// question: how did Ken test whether the reasoning could actually find
// problems whose answers were already known? Deliberately excludes the
// $251K/Evidence Trail material, the 11-table/22-test schema and
// constraint-suite detail, the closing diagnostic's full reasoning, and any
// V0.3 discussion — those live elsewhere per the brief's Decision 2/3 and
// §8. Video 2 (Technical Practitioner) is a reserved placeholder, now
// living in the Hero's two-zone read-or-watch layout; production is
// Workstream G. Major sections now alternate light/navy per the
// browser-review correction (Home's established rhythm), applied to this
// page only — see the frontmatter note on other Workstream F pages before
// assuming this rule applies there without its own sign-off.
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';

const sequenceSteps = [
  'Ground Truth frozen',
  'Evaluation criteria frozen',
  'Blind procedure designed/audited',
  'Fresh isolated sessions',
  'Outputs frozen',
  'Scoring',
  'MISS / MISS / CLEAN',
];
---

<Layout title="Methodology &amp; Evaluation — Ken Corioso | Harbor Ridge V1">
  <main>
    <!-- Hero (LIGHT) -->
    <section class="section section--hero">
      <div class="shell">
        <p class="eyebrow">Methodology &amp; Evaluation</p>
        <h1 class="page-h1">
          <span class="page-h1__lead">I already knew the answers.</span>
          <span class="page-h1__continuation">The question was whether AI could find them.</span>
        </h1>
        <div class="hero-row">
          <p class="lead hero-row__copy">
            The executive problem wasn't confined to marketing, admissions,
            finance, or operations. So I designed the analytical environment
            around the relationships between them. The Evidence Engine had
            access to a relational representation of Harbor Ridge spanning
            acquisition, inquiry, financial qualification, admission,
            treatment and revenue. I wanted the analysis to distinguish
            different kinds of performance problems rather than assume that
            declining admissions automatically meant an admissions problem.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-row__media">
            <div class="video-frame" role="img" aria-label="Video placeholder: Video 2, Technical Practitioner — reserved, not yet produced">
              <span class="video-frame__play" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="video-frame__caption">Video 2 — Technical Practitioner</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Freezing the Rules (NAVY) -->
    <section class="section section--dark">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="editorial">
          <div class="editorial__label">
            <h2 class="section-heading section-heading--on-dark">Freezing the Rules</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="editorial__body measure">
            <p class="on-dark-body">
              For the blind evaluation, I went further. I froze Ground Truth
              before AI analysis began. The answer key was based on the
              actual generated scenarios, and the rule was explicit: what
              counted as the correct answer could not change based on what
              the AI later found or missed.
            </p>
            <p class="on-dark-body">
              That created a clean separation between two questions:
              <strong>did the analysis surface something useful?</strong> and
              <strong>did it recover the deliberately hidden problem it was
              being tested to find?</strong> Those questions eventually
              produced different answers.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Designing the Blind Evaluation (LIGHT) -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="editorial">
          <div class="editorial__label">
            <h2 class="section-heading">Designing the Blind Evaluation</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="editorial__body measure">
            <p>
              After the first blind-analysis attempt produced mixed results, I
              redesigned the evaluation. For V0.2, I froze an Evaluation
              Interpretation Protocol defining Pass/Partial/Miss for known
              scenarios and Clean/Borderline/False Positive for a Healthy
              Baseline negative control.
            </p>
            <p>
              The discovery procedure was designed without Harbor Ridge
              context. I subjected it to two independent genericity audits.
              Both returned 10/10 PASS. Only then did I freeze the procedure
              and run three fresh, isolated blind sessions: Scenario 1,
              Scenario 2, and the Healthy Baseline. The outputs were frozen
              before scoring.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="shell">
        <div class="process" role="group" aria-label="The methodology sequence, in order: Ground Truth frozen, evaluation criteria frozen, blind procedure designed and audited, fresh isolated sessions, outputs frozen, scoring, MISS MISS CLEAN">
          <div class="process__rail" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="process__rail-fill"></span>
            {sequenceSteps.map(() => (
              <span class="process__tick"></span>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="process__grid">
            {sequenceSteps.map((step, i) => (
              <div class:list={['process__node', { 'process__node--result': i === sequenceSteps.length - 1 }]}>
                <span class="process__label">{step}</span>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Result (NAVY — frozen, visually unchanged) -->
    <section class="section section--navy">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="editorial">
          <div class="editorial__label">
            <h2 class="section-heading section-heading--on-dark">The Result</h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <dl class="reckoning">
          <div class="reckoning__item">
            <dt>Scenario 1</dt>
            <dd>MISS</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="reckoning__item">
            <dt>Scenario 2</dt>
            <dd>MISS</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="reckoning__item">
            <dt>Healthy Baseline</dt>
            <dd>CLEAN</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>

        <div class="editorial editorial--continuation">
          <div class="editorial__body measure">
            <p class="on-dark-lead">
              The misses were not cases where the system simply found
              nothing. In both scenarios, it found and prioritized other
              patterns that substantially contradicted the frozen Ground
              Truth. The Healthy Baseline remained clean, which is useful
              evidence about that control test.
              <strong>It does not prove general reliability.</strong>
            </p>
            <p class="on-dark-lead">
              I designed the evaluation so the Evidence Engine could fail
              without letting me redefine failure afterward. Then it did.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What It Means and What It Doesn't (LIGHT) -->
    <section class="section section--quiet">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="editorial">
          <div class="editorial__label">
            <h2 class="section-heading">What It Means and What It Doesn't</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="editorial__body measure">
            <p>
              The specific V0.2 discovery procedure was insufficient to
              reliably recover the previously demonstrated localized failures
              under the existing Harbor Ridge experimental conditions.
            </p>
            <p>
              That conclusion is intentionally narrow. The evaluation showed
              that this procedure did not reliably recover the planted
              failures under these conditions. It did not erase the useful
              findings the analysis surfaced elsewhere, and the Healthy
              Baseline's CLEAN result did not establish general reliability.
            </p>
            <p>
              A subsequent diagnostic examined why the misses may have
              occurred and found evidence consistent with signal-to-noise
              structure in the experimental environment. That analysis was
              informative, but not decisive. I therefore preserved the
              benchmark result rather than changing the evaluation after
              seeing it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Go Deeper (NAVY) -->
    <section class="section section--deeper section--dark">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="editorial">
          <div class="editorial__label">
            <h2 class="section-heading section-heading--on-dark">Go Deeper</h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <ol class="index-list">
          <li class="index-list__item">
            <a href="/full-methodology">
              <span class="index-list__num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
              <span class="index-list__content">
                <span class="index-list__title">Full Methodology</span>
                <span class="index-list__desc">
                  the complete technical account — reserved, not yet published
                </span>
              </span>
              <span class="index-list__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li class="index-list__item">
            <a href="/portability-lessons">
              <span class="index-list__num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
              <span class="index-list__content">
                <span class="index-list__title">Portability &amp; Lessons</span>
                <span class="index-list__desc">the closing diagnostic's full reasoning</span>
              </span>
              <span class="index-list__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
       Canvas/measure/rhythm transferred from the frozen Home/Evidence
       visual system, redeclared here since Astro scopes each page's own
       styles. No new palette, spacing, or type-scale values introduced.
       --------------------------------------------------------------- */
    .shell {
      max-width: 1280px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    }

    .shell + .shell {
      margin-top: var(--space-5);
    }

    .measure {
      max-width: 68ch;
    }

    .section {
      padding: clamp(var(--space-7), 9vw, var(--space-8)) 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-slate-border);
    }

    main > .section:last-of-type {
      border-bottom: none;
    }

    .section-heading {
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: var(--text-h2);
      line-height: var(--line-height-heading-sub);
      color: var(--color-sovereign-navy);
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-4) 0;
    }

    .section-heading--on-dark {
      color: var(--color-white);
    }

    .section p {
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-4) 0;
    }

    .section p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: var(--text-small);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      color: var(--color-slate-text-secondary);
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-4) 0;
    }

    .page-h1 {
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 2vw, var(--text-h1));
      line-height: var(--line-height-heading);
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-6) 0;
    }

    .page-h1__lead {
      color: var(--color-sovereign-navy);
    }

    .page-h1__continuation {
      color: var(--color-quantum-electric-blue);
    }

    .lead {
      font-size: var(--text-lead);
      color: var(--color-slate-text-secondary);
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
       Dark-section canvas — Sovereign Navy. Was previously referenced
       in markup (Go Deeper) without ever being declared in this page's
       own scoped styles, so Go Deeper rendered with white heading text
       on the page's default light canvas. Declared here (matching
       Home's/Evidence's own per-page redeclaration, since Astro scopes
       CSS per file) and now also used by Freezing the Rules.
       --------------------------------------------------------------- */
    .section--dark {
      background: var(--color-sovereign-navy);
      border-bottom: none;
    }

    .section--dark :focus-visible {
      outline-color: var(--color-quantum-electric-blue);
    }

    .on-dark-body {
      color: var(--color-navy-muted-on-dark);
    }

    .on-dark-lead {
      font-size: var(--text-lead);
      color: var(--color-navy-muted-on-dark);
    }

    .on-dark-body strong,
    .on-dark-lead strong {
      color: var(--color-white);
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
       Editorial row — the site-wide label-rail-plus-body device,
       redeclared at the same breakpoint/values as Home's and Evidence's.
       --------------------------------------------------------------- */
    .editorial {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      row-gap: var(--space-4);
    }

    .editorial__label .section-heading {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    @media (min-width: 900px) {
      .editorial {
        grid-template-columns: minmax(160px, 20%) minmax(0, 1fr);
        column-gap: var(--space-6);
        align-items: start;
      }

      .editorial--continuation .editorial__body {
        grid-column: 2;
      }
    }

    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
       Hero — full-width H1, then the same asymmetric copy/media row
       Home's Hero uses (read-or-watch: the supporting explanation on
       the left, Video 2's reserved placeholder on the right, joined by
       one connective vertical rule at the desktop breakpoint). Values
       transferred from Home's .hero-row rather than reinvented.
       --------------------------------------------------------------- */
    .section--hero {
      padding-top: clamp(var(--space-6), 8vw, var(--space-8));
      padding-bottom: clamp(var(--space-7), 8vw, var(--space-8));
    }

    .hero-row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-6);
      align-items: start;
    }

    .hero-row__copy {
      max-width: 60ch;
    }

    @media (min-width: 1100px) {
      .hero-row {
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 3fr) minmax(0, 2fr);
        align-items: center;
      }

      .hero-row__media {
        padding-left: var(--space-6);
        border-left: 1px solid var(--color-slate-border);
      }
    }

    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
       Video frame — Video 2 (Technical Practitioner), transferred
       unchanged from Home's video-object pattern. Non-interactive
       role="img" with an honest placeholder label; no controls implying
       playable media exists.
       --------------------------------------------------------------- */
    .video-frame {
      position: relative;
      width: 100%;
      aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
      background: var(--color-sovereign-navy);
      color: var(--color-white);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: var(--space-3);
      border-radius: 16px;
    }

    .video-frame__play {
      display: inline-block;
      width: 0;
      height: 0;
      border-top: 16px solid transparent;
      border-bottom: 16px solid transparent;
      border-left: 26px solid var(--color-white);
      margin-left: 6px;
    }

    .video-frame__caption {
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: var(--text-small);
      letter-spacing: 0.03em;
      text-align: center;
      padding: 0 var(--space-4);
    }

    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
       Designing the Blind Evaluation — process graphic. Same visual
       grammar as Home's frozen "What I Built" Golden Thread (bounded,
       elevated container; a continuous connecting rail with one tick
       per stage; connected nodes reading as a resolved, orderly
       progression) — deliberately not Home's "The Problem" broken-chain
       treatment, which communicates disconnection and would be the
       wrong meaning here. Seven stages instead of Golden Thread's four;
       the final stage (the benchmark outcome) gets a filled navy tag so
       the MISS/MISS/CLEAN endpoint reads as the graphic's destination,
       without color-coding it as good or bad.
       --------------------------------------------------------------- */
    .process {
      position: relative;
      background: var(--color-steel-gray-surface);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-5) var(--space-5);
    }

    .process__rail {
      position: relative;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(7, 1fr);
      height: 20px;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }

    .process__rail-fill {
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      top: 50%;
      height: 2px;
      background: var(--color-sovereign-navy);
      transform: translateY(-50%);
    }

    .process__tick {
      justify-self: center;
      align-self: center;
      width: 9px;
      height: 9px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--color-sovereign-navy);
      z-index: 1;
    }

    .process__grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(7, 1fr);
      column-gap: var(--space-3);
    }

    .process__node {
      padding: 0 var(--space-3) 0 0;
      border-left: 1px solid var(--color-slate-border);
      padding-left: var(--space-3);
    }

    .process__node:first-child {
      padding-left: 0;
      border-left: none;
    }

    .process__label {
      display: block;
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: var(--text-small);
      line-height: 1.3;
      color: var(--color-sovereign-navy);
    }

    .process__node--result .process__label {
      display: inline-block;
      font-size: var(--text-small);
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      color: var(--color-white);
      background: var(--color-sovereign-navy);
      padding: 0.25em var(--space-2);
      border-radius: 4px;
    }

    /* Below the Golden Thread's own breakpoint: rail hidden, nodes
       become a vertical connected-rail list (dot per node, one shared
       left border), exactly Home's mobile fallback for the same
       component — chosen over forcing 7 narrow horizontal columns,
       which would harm readability rather than communicate order. */
    @media (max-width: 899px) {
      .process {
        padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-4);
      }

      .process__rail {
        display: none;
      }

      .process__grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        row-gap: var(--space-4);
        border-left: 2px solid var(--color-sovereign-navy);
      }

      .process__node {
        position: relative;
        padding: 0 0 0 var(--space-4);
        border-left: none;
      }

      .process__node:first-child {
        padding-left: var(--space-4);
      }

      .process__node::before {
        content: '';
        position: absolute;
        left: -5px;
        top: 0.35em;
        width: 9px;
        height: 9px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: var(--color-sovereign-navy);
      }
    }

    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
       The Result — the page's one Sovereign Navy reckoning, same
       component pattern already proven on Home (dl.reckoning): MISS /
       MISS / CLEAN with genuinely equal visual weight, no color-coding.
       Frozen per Ken's approval — unchanged in this pass.
       --------------------------------------------------------------- */
    .section--navy {
      background: var(--color-sovereign-navy);
      border-bottom: none;
      padding-top: clamp(var(--space-7), 10vw, var(--space-8));
      padding-bottom: clamp(var(--space-7), 10vw, var(--space-8));
    }

    .section--navy :focus-visible {
      outline-color: var(--color-quantum-electric-blue);
    }

    .reckoning {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      margin: var(--space-6) 0 clamp(var(--space-7), 8vw, var(--space-8)) 0;
      padding: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-navy-muted-on-dark);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-navy-muted-on-dark);
    }

    .reckoning__item {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      padding: var(--space-5) 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-navy-muted-on-dark);
    }

    .reckoning__item:first-child {
      border-top: none;
    }

    .reckoning__item dt {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: var(--text-small);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      color: var(--color-navy-muted-on-dark);
      margin: 0;
    }

    .reckoning__item dd {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 2.4rem + 6vw, 8rem);
      line-height: 1;
      color: var(--color-white);
      letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    }

    @media (min-width: 640px) {
      .reckoning {
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
        padding: var(--space-6) 0;
        container-type: inline-size;
      }

      .reckoning__item {
        border-top: none;
        padding: 0 var(--space-5);
        border-left: 1px solid var(--color-navy-muted-on-dark);
      }

      .reckoning__item:first-child {
        padding-left: 0;
        border-left: none;
      }

      /* Same 958px-overflow fix Home's reckoning uses: size against the
         container's own measured width (cqi), not viewport width (vw),
         so the three equal-weight results don't overflow their column
         at intermediate widths. */
      .reckoning__item dd {
        font-size: clamp(2.5rem, -2.36rem + 14cqi, 8rem);
      }
    }

    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
       What It Means and What It Doesn't — deliberately calm after the
       dark reckoning, same emotional logic as Home's "What This
       Demonstrates".
       --------------------------------------------------------------- */
    .section--quiet {
      padding-top: clamp(var(--space-7), 9vw, var(--space-8));
    }

    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
       Go Deeper — same indexed-list family as Home's. Full Methodology
       now links to its reserved route (/full-methodology); its
       supporting copy stays "reserved, not yet published" until that
       route holds a real, provenance-verified page.
       --------------------------------------------------------------- */
    .section--deeper {
      padding-bottom: clamp(var(--space-8), 10vw, calc(var(--space-8) * 1.2));
      /* The shared site footer (Layout.astro) adds its own space-8
         margin-top after this, the page's last section. Left alone, that
         renders as a visible light-canvas band between this dark section
         and the footer. Canceling the footer's margin here (page-scoped,
         Layout.astro untouched) — the same technique already used on
         /evidence and /evidence-trail's own last section — lets the navy
         background transition directly into the footer. */
      margin-bottom: calc(-1 * var(--space-8));
    }

    .index-list {
      list-style: none;
      margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-4) 0;
      padding: 0;
    }

    .index-list__item {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-navy-muted-on-dark);
    }

    .index-list__item:last-child {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-navy-muted-on-dark);
    }

    .index-list__item a {
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: var(--space-5);
      padding: var(--space-5) 0;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--color-white);
      min-height: 44px;
    }

    .index-list__num {
      flex-shrink: 0;
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: var(--text-h3);
      color: var(--color-navy-muted-on-dark);
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      min-width: 2ch;
    }

    .index-list__content {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-1);
      flex: 1 1 auto;
      min-width: 0;
    }

    .index-list__item a:hover .index-list__title,
    .index-list__item a:focus-visible .index-list__title {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .index-list__title {
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: var(--text-body);
    }

    .index-list__desc {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: var(--text-small);
      color: var(--color-navy-muted-on-dark);
    }

    .index-list__arrow {
      flex-shrink: 0;
      color: var(--color-navy-muted-on-dark);
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateX(-4px);
      transition: opacity 200ms ease, transform 200ms ease;
    }

    .index-list__item a:hover .index-list__arrow,
    .index-list__item a:focus-visible .index-list__arrow {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateX(0);
      color: var(--color-white);
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .index-list__arrow {
        transition: none !important;
      }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
